        "original_id": "68b33dad-d023-5af2-a374-1d0f9f9b0070",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: qutebrowser, DuckDuckGo\n- Platforms: Linux, Windows, macOS\n- Concepts: vim-style key bindings, minimal GUI, default search engine, search result sourcing\n\nFacts:\n- qutebrowser is a web browser for Linux, Windows, and macOS.\n- qutebrowser has vim-style key bindings and a minimal GUI.\n- qutebrowser uses DuckDuckGo as its default search engine.\n- DuckDuckGo emphasizes returning the best results rather than the most results.\n- DuckDuckGo generates search results from more than 400 individual sources.\n- DuckDuckGo includes Wikipedia, Bing, Yahoo!, Yandex, and Yummly among its search result sources.",
